{:hole/id :apm-review-dispatch-resolution-witness
 :hole/status :open
 :opened-at "2026-08-25"
 :opened-by "claude-12"
 :authority :apm-cycle-machine-lean
 :introduced-by "mathlib4-apm-validation b5d6d08edc (Model resolvable promotion review dispatches)"

 :reason
 "ValidReviewDispatch makes unreviewable material unconstructible, and
  valid_dispatch_excludes_apparatus_failure proves the six apparatus causes
  uninhabited from a valid dispatch. But the resolution witnesses are
  self-reported booleans -- candidatePersisted, candidateFetchable,
  parentPatternFetchable, baseProblemBlobFetchable, solverFinalHeadFetchable,
  and per-trace fetchable are fields someone fills in. Nothing ties
  candidatePersisted = true to the candidate actually being persisted. So the
  model currently proves: IF the controller says everything resolves, THEN the
  enumerated failures do not occur. That is the F32 shape one layer out --
  TN-fable-F32-model section 2, 'Lean verifies that Clojure reports its own
  hand-written schema as satisfied' -- and it is declared here rather than
  discovered later, because a hole that is named bounds what the validation
  claims. The dispatch precondition is sound UP TO THIS HOLE."

 :intended-closure
 "Replace each boolean assertion with a content-addressed witness, the move
  already idiomatic in this model: APMCampaignTraceChecker's TraceReviewSnapshot
  carries snapshotDigest and contentDigest and requires them equal, so a named
  snapshot is content-addressed rather than merely non-empty (26b3ba9668 and
  d996dde673). Resolution should be witnessed the same way -- the fetched
  content's digest, which the id determines -- so that a controller cannot
  assert resolution it did not perform."

 :sequencing
 "Closes with the Clojure enforcement packet rather than before it. That packet
  is where the controller must actually PRODUCE the resolution record, and so
  is where the field is decided to be a claim or a witness. Splitting them
  would land a Lean witness type with no producer, which is the defect class
  this campaign exists to remove."

 :closure-test
 "ReviewCandidateResolution and ReviewerInputResolution carry content digests
  rather than booleans; a dispatch whose asserted digest does not match the
  fetched content is not constructible as ValidReviewDispatch; the Clojure
  controller derives those digests from the fetch it performed, and a test
  shows a fabricated digest is refused."}
